e shared root set: a new `reachable-values` returns the cell table, **every frame's registers**, every pending (whose own values include the retained `:put` datom, the `:ffi-request` envelope, and the link envelope), the store, the module stores, the parked records, and the halt result — and `tagged-of` walks map **keys and values both**, so a sealed reference sitting as a store key or literal entry is found too. The pendings' own `:yin.k/cell`/`:yin.k/response-cell` fields still count directly. A cell the encoder minted inside wait-frame registers or an envelope is therefore no `:extra-cell`.\n\n### P1-2 — stream markers across the complete graph\n`resume-task` now attaches `body-markers`: every `:yin.k/stream` marker in that same `reachable-values` set (replacing the old cells-plus-selected-pendings collection), deduplicated by identity inside `attach-all!`. A stream carried solely in a store, closure, register, parked record or the halt result is attached exactly like one a pending names, so the decoder's re-sealed reference resolves.\n\n### P1-3 — child install validation and refusal propagation\n`validate-body`'s installs pass now recursively validates each `:yin.k/child` with `validate-body` itself (decoded CBOR is a tree, so the recursion terminates), before any attachment or restoration. `resume-installs` checks the child's `resume-task` outcome and throws the child's refusal — the parent's `call!` converts it to that data outcome, and since the throw lands before any machine value is assembled, the parent never answers `:ok` over a child that did not lower.\n\n### P1-4 — frame and register validation\n`validate-body` enforces non-empty frames on `:blocked`; `validate-registers` checks field types (`:yin.k/pc` a non-negative integer inside the segment's length, `:yin.k/env` a map, `:yin.k/stack` and `:yin.k/k` vectors) beside presence and segment membership; and the new `check-frame-pc` re-proves on the bytes what the lift proved on the live entry — the resume pc must sit at a static safepoint (`ucf/safepoint-at`) whose `:yin.safepoint/kinds` admit the pending's wire reason, refusing `:yin.k/undecodable` (kind `:reason-mismatch` for an inadmissible reason).\n\n### New test coverage (4 deftests, 17→21 tests, 107→131 assertions)\n- A cell reachable **only** through a wait frame's captured environment, and one reachable only through a retained FFI envelope's argument, both export without `:extra-cell`, appear in the body, and lower `:ok`.\n- A stream reference carried only in a register and the store attaches at the lower, and the re-sealed reference resolves to a live reflection in the receiver's resources.\n- A refused install child aborts the parent both ways: a grammar-broken child (empty child code) is caught by the recursive validation before attachment (`:yin.k/undecodable`), and a child whose cell's route cannot attach propagates `:yin.k/unsatisfied` with the parent not `:ok`.\n- The frame battery: `:blocked` without frames (missing and empty), out-of-bounds pc (9999), negative pc, a resume pc at no safepoint (pc 0 of the reader program), a reason the pc's kinds do not admit (`:reason-mismatch`), and register fields of the wrong type (env as a vector, stack as a map).\n\n### Verification\n- **JVM:** `Ran 2860 tests containing 225982 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.` (2,856/225,947 before this round; +4 tests/+35 assertions are the new coverage)\n- **Node:** `Ran 2677 tests containing 91397 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.` (2,673/91,370 before)\n- clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings and cljstyle clean on both touched files; every line ≤ 80 columns, pure ASCII, no em dashes. Nothing committed or staged; the tree still carries only the stage-1 files plus this round's edits to the two permitted files.\n\nStatus: COMPLETE\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790968778707-reviewer-linker-hardening-stage1-r5-gate.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790875163601-vm-engineer-hardening-stage1-kept-cursor.glm-5.3.stdout-r5.log\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
