{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-02 19:21:31 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-03 02:21:31 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nThree prior P1 fixes are closed; frame validation remains incomplete.\n\n- **P1 — Missing segment bypasses validation.** `validate-registers` does not require `:yin.k/segment`, and bounds and safepoint checks run only when it exists ([handoff.cljc:824](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-hardening/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc:824), [handoff.cljc:850](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-hardening/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc:850)). Removing the segment and setting pc to 9999 therefore passes validation and lowers successfully without a segment. Require a non-nil segment naming carried code, then check bounds and eligibility unconditionally. Add missing/nil-segment cases.\n\n- **P1 — Parked records bypass safepoint validation.** Their validation invokes only `validate-registers` ([handoff.cljc:976](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-hardening/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc:976)). An in-bounds ordinary instruction pc is accepted and restored as a parked continuation. Require the explicit-park safepoint kind for parked records; add tampering coverage.\n\n- **P2 — Stream regression test does not isolate the defect.** The carried stream is taken from the existing reader’s `:stream-id` ([handoff_test.cljc:1121](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-hardening/test/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_test.cljc:1121)). Its pending cell already forces attachment, so the old collector would also pass. Use a distinct stream reachable solely through the tested value roots.\n\nThe cell traversal now covers registers and envelopes ([handoff.cljc:887](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-hardening/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc:887)); stream collection uses those same roots and deduplicates by identity ([handoff.cljc:1026](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-hardening/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc:1026)). Child bodies are recursively validated, and child refusals propagate ([handoff.cljc:978](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-hardening/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc:978), [handoff.cljc:1146](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-hardening/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc:1146)).\n\nNo unrelated scope creep found. Accepted the supplied JVM/Node results and verified the correct Dart log ends at **2,632, all passed**, including all 21 handoff tests. No files edited or suites rerun.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED"}}
